- op: discuss  # 9f5e
  at: '2026-07-21T21:16:35Z'  # 9f5e
  by: agent  # 9f5e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9f5e
  clock: 4  # 9f5e
  nonce: 9f5e  # 9f5e
  message: "wont_do 2026-07-21 (staleness audit). The behavior reproduces verbatim (rust.py:1051 id_name_segment = full_name.replace('::','.') feeds the id name-slot while node.name = full_name keeps native '::'), BUT this is BY DESIGN, not a defect: ADR-0036 Ruling-1 blesses name-slot ':'->'.' sanitization as the intended-lossy contract (canonical ids forbid ':' in the name segment per ADR-0034 Phase-6; full fidelity lives in Symbol.name). The item post-dates the 2026-06-10 ADR-0036 ruling, so its 'separator-normalization bug' premise is superseded by the accepted design. Not a code-fix candidate; closing as wont_do/by-design. If a non-lossy Rust escaping is ever wanted, that would be a fresh design item, not this bug."  # 9f5e
